# Demos are wiring

Package `demo/` **composes** the library. It does not own session machines,
tree walks, flatten/sync, or other domain rules.

## What a demo may do

- Call library hooks / HOCs (`makeUseDialogs`, `useFlatListSession`,
  `useFollowUpAdd`, `followUpDraftsList`, …)
- Pass host chrome (render props, labels, fixtures)
- Seed Storybook `INITIAL_*` data

## What a demo must not do

- Reimplement a library orchestrator (item/section sessions, `commitDraft`,
  extra-map walks, flatten/sync)
- Invent flags that hide host composition (`embedded` instead of
  `sidebar: ReactNode | null`)
- Duplicate generic HTML that belongs in `src/demo-utils/`

Heavy logic is either **extracted** (reusable, no HTML) or **removed** by
twisting the library so the demo can just wire it.

## `src/demo-utils/` vs form chrome

Generic widgets that could live in an external UI kit go in
[`src/demo-utils/`](../../src/demo-utils): page shell, sidebar layout,
confirm banner, dropdown **including the popover panel**. Import them only
from `demo/` and `*.stories.tsx` — never from library `_deps` / package
source. Hosts pass the trigger and items; they do not restyle the panel.

One file per widget (`DemoPage.tsx`, `DropdownMenu.tsx`, …). `index.ts`
only re-exports. Do not dump components into `index.tsx`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — package demo owns popover chrome
<div style={{ position: "absolute", background: "#fff", boxShadow: … }}>
  {items}
</div>

// ✅ GOOD — DropdownMenu owns the panel
<DropdownMenu open={open} align="end" trigger={icon}>
  {items}
</DropdownMenu>
```

Form-specific chrome stays in package demos and is **imported**, not copied
(`RequiredMark`, `sectionChrome`, `FollowUpAdd`). See
`unify-demo-chrome.mdc`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — demo walks the tree and brands extras
const map = new Map();
const walk = (cols) => { … map.set(item.header.id, branded({…})) };

// ✅ GOOD — library walk; host brands at the leaf
extrasByItemId(sections, (item) => branded({ actions: itemActions(item) }))
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — boolean hides two host layouts
<FormDialogsEditor embedded={true} />

// ✅ GOOD — host names the empty chrome
<FormDialogsEditor sidebar={null} />
```

Related: `no-html-outside-demo.mdc`, `unify-demo-chrome.mdc`,
`no-zero-responsibility.mdc`.
